bench_loop_taken — 1% without BTB vs 98% with BTB 

x1 = 100
loop:
  x1 = x1 - 1
  BNE x1, x0, loop   
 ← is x1 ≠ 0? YES → TAKEN (99 times), only NOT taken at the end

Without BTB: 99 wrong out of 100 → only 1% correct
With BTB: After the first miss, the 2-bit counter goes to state 2 (weakly taken), then 3 (strongly taken). Every iteration 2–99 is correctly predicted taken. Only iteration 1 (first miss) and iteration 100 (exit, predicted taken but not-taken) are wrong → 2 mispredictions → 98%